IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fhog-core`

-- First Home Owner Grant and Other Home Owner Grants Act 2000 (Qld) -- the first home buyer's questions.
--
-- SEAT: the first home buyer, the applicant for a first home owner grant (s 16), who is or will be an owner of the
-- home (s 17). "Is the home I am buying or building eligible? Am I eligible? How much will I get? By when must I apply,
-- move in, and for how long must I stay? What happens if I do not, and what can I be made to repay? How do I object?"
-- Every question is phrased as that person would ask it, on facts that person could state. The rules are in
-- fhog-core.l4; this module builds the core's records from plain answers and restates no rule.
--
-- SHARED INPUTS. The transaction questions take the same twenty answers in the same order, and the applicant questions
-- the same twenty-four, so the form can ask each once. A joint applicant asks the applicant questions from their own
-- seat; the payable question asks only whether the other applicant meets criteria 1 to 4.
--
-- DATES. A purchase or build that commenced before 20 November 2023 is governed by a version of the Act that is not
-- deposited (s 91, and ss 79 to 81 for 2012): the transaction, amount and payable questions answer `not covered`.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `First home owner grant -- the first home buyer's questions`

§§ `Building the core's records from my answers`

GIVEN `what I am doing`                                                        IS A `Kind of transaction`
      `the home is a building fixed to land`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `the home may lawfully be lived in`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
      `the home is suitable to live in`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
      `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before`                    IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises for GST`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `as renovated, the home has been lived in or sold as a home before`      IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Home facts`
`my home from my answers` `what I am doing` `the home is a building fixed to land` `the home may lawfully be lived in` `the home is suitable to live in` `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` `the sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises for GST` `as renovated, the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` MEANS
    `Home facts` WITH
        `is a building fixed to land`                                          IS `the home is a building fixed to land`
        `may lawfully be used as a place of residence`                         IS `the home may lawfully be lived in`
        `is a suitable building for use as a place of residence`               IS `the home is suitable to live in`
        `has been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence`         IS `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before`
        `is the subject of a contract for its purchase`                        IS `it is a purchase`
        `its sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises under GST Act s 40-75(1)(b)` IS `the sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises for GST`
        `as renovated, has been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence` IS `as renovated, the home has been lived in or sold as a home before`
    WHERE
        `it is a purchase` MEANS
            CONSIDER `what I am doing`
            WHEN `a contract to buy a home` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `what I am doing`                                                        IS A `Kind of transaction`
      `the home is in Queensland`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
      `the home is a building fixed to land`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `the home may lawfully be lived in`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
      `the home is suitable to live in`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
      `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before`                    IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises for GST`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `as renovated, the home has been lived in or sold as a home before`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am buying land with the home on it, or that the seller will build on before completion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller is building the home before completion`                      IS A BOOLEAN
      `I own the land, or will own it on completion of the contract`           IS A BOOLEAN
      `the commencement date`                                                  IS A DATE
      `the consideration`                                                      IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the home`                                                  IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the land`                                                  IS A NUMBER
      `the Commissioner has found the contract is part of a scheme to get around the grant's limits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an option or right to the contract was granted before 1 July 2000`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract replaces one made before 20 November 2023 for the same or a similar home` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an option or right to the contract was granted before 20 November 2023` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner is satisfied the earlier option, right or contract is not part of a scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner has found the contract is part of a scheme to get the 2023 to 2026 amount` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Transaction facts`
`my transaction from my answers` `what I am doing` `the home is in Queensland` `the home is a building fixed to land` `the home may lawfully be lived in` `the home is suitable to live in` `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` `the sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises for GST` `as renovated, the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` `I am buying land with the home on it, or that the seller will build on before completion` `the seller is building the home before completion` `I own the land, or will own it on completion of the contract` `the commencement date` `the consideration` `the value of the home` `the value of the land` `the Commissioner has found the contract is part of a scheme to get around the grant's limits` `an option or right to the contract was granted before 1 July 2000` `the contract replaces one made before 20 November 2023 for the same or a similar home` `an option or right to the contract was granted before 20 November 2023` `the Commissioner is satisfied the earlier option, right or contract is not part of a scheme` `the Commissioner has found the contract is part of a scheme to get the 2023 to 2026 amount` MEANS
    `Transaction facts` WITH
        `kind`                                                                 IS `what I am doing`
        `the home is in Queensland`                                            IS `the home is in Queensland`
        `the home`                                                             IS `my home from my answers` `what I am doing` `the home is a building fixed to land` `the home may lawfully be lived in` `the home is suitable to live in` `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` `the sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises for GST` `as renovated, the home has been lived in or sold as a home before`
        `the contract is for a relevant interest in land with the home on it, or to be built on it by or for the vendor at the vendor's expense` IS `I am buying land with the home on it, or that the seller will build on before completion`
        `the home is to be built by or for the vendor before completion`       IS `the seller is building the home before completion`
        `the person building owns the land, or will own it on completion`     IS `I own the land, or will own it on completion of the contract`
        `the commencement date`                                                IS `the commencement date`
        `the consideration`                                                    IS `the consideration`
        `the unencumbered value of the home`                                   IS `the value of the home`
        `the unencumbered value of the land at the commencement date`          IS `the value of the land`
        `the commissioner is satisfied the contract is part of a scheme (s 5(4))` IS `the Commissioner has found the contract is part of a scheme to get around the grant's limits`
        `an option or right to the contract was granted before 1 July 2000`    IS `an option or right to the contract was granted before 1 July 2000`
        `the commissioner is satisfied there is no scheme despite s 5(5)`      IS `the Commissioner is satisfied the earlier option, right or contract is not part of a scheme`
        `the commissioner is satisfied the contract is part of a scheme (s 25EA(2))` IS `the Commissioner has found the contract is part of a scheme to get the 2023 to 2026 amount`
        `the contract replaces a contract made before 20 November 2023 for the same or a substantially similar home` IS `the contract replaces one made before 20 November 2023 for the same or a similar home`
        `an option or right to the contract was granted before 20 November 2023` IS `an option or right to the contract was granted before 20 November 2023`
        `the commissioner is satisfied there is no scheme despite s 25EA(3)`   IS `the Commissioner is satisfied the earlier option, right or contract is not part of a scheme`

GIVEN `I was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `that grant was paid back because it was not payable, with any penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Earlier grant facts`
`an earlier grant from my answers` `I was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid` `that grant was paid back because it was not payable, with any penalty` MEANS
    `Earlier grant facts` WITH
        `was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid`     IS `I was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid`
        `that grant was paid back because s 10(1) was not satisfied, with any s 47 penalty` IS `that grant was paid back because it was not payable, with any penalty`

GIVEN `held an interest in a home before 1 July 2000`                          IS A BOOLEAN
      `that interest was only as an instalment buyer, ended within a year, without the title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `since 1 July 2000 held an interest in another home that I or my spouse lived in` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that home was in my earlier application, and I repaid that grant for not living there long enough` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Earlier property facts`
`an earlier property from my answers` `held an interest in a home before 1 July 2000` `that interest was only as an instalment buyer, ended within a year, without the title` `since 1 July 2000 held an interest in another home that I or my spouse lived in` `that home was in my earlier application, and I repaid that grant for not living there long enough` MEANS
    `Earlier property facts` WITH
        `held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000` IS `held an interest in a home before 1 July 2000`
        `that interest was as purchaser by instalments, the contract ended within 1 year and the fee simple was not acquired` IS `that interest was only as an instalment buyer, ended within a year, without the title`
        `held, from 1 July 2000 and before the application, a relevant interest in other residential property used as the residence of the applicant or spouse` IS `since 1 July 2000 held an interest in another home that I or my spouse lived in`
        `that property was the subject of the applicant's earlier application whose grant was repaid for failing criterion 5` IS `that home was in my earlier application, and I repaid that grant for not living there long enough`

GIVEN `my relationship`                                                        IS A `Relationship`
      `my partner and I live together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the years my partner and I have lived together as a couple`             IS A NUMBER
      `my partner and I live apart`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner is satisfied we have no intention of living together again` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner is satisfied we intend to live together again`         IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Partner facts`
`my partner from my answers` `my relationship` `my partner and I live together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis` `the years my partner and I have lived together as a couple` `my partner and I live apart` `the Commissioner is satisfied we have no intention of living together again` `the Commissioner is satisfied we intend to live together again` MEANS
    `Partner facts` WITH
        `the relationship`                                                     IS `my relationship`
        `they are living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis`     IS `my partner and I live together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis`
        `the years they have lived together as a couple`                       IS `the years my partner and I have lived together as a couple`
        `they are living apart`                                                IS `my partner and I live apart`
        `the commissioner is satisfied they have no intention of again living together as a couple` IS `the Commissioner is satisfied we have no intention of living together again`
        `the commissioner is satisfied they intend to again live together as a couple` IS `the Commissioner is satisfied we intend to live together again`

GIVEN `I am applying as an individual`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
      `my age on the commencement date`                                        IS A NUMBER
      `the Commissioner has exempted me from the age requirement`              IS A BOOLEAN
      `my citizenship or residence`                                            IS A `Citizenship or residence`
      `I am applying with another person`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `that grant was paid back because it was not payable, with any penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I held an interest in a home before 1 July 2000`                        IS A BOOLEAN
      `my interest was only as an instalment buyer, ended within a year, without the title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `since 1 July 2000 I held an interest in another home that I or my spouse lived in` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that home was in my earlier application, and I repaid that grant for not living there long enough` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my relationship`                                                        IS A `Relationship`
      `my partner and I live together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the years my partner and I have lived together as a couple`             IS A NUMBER
      `my partner and I live apart`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner is satisfied we have no intention of living together again` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner is satisfied we intend to live together again`         IS A BOOLEAN
      `my partner was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my partner's grant was paid back because it was not payable, with any penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my partner held an interest in a home before 1 July 2000`               IS A BOOLEAN
      `my partner's interest was only as an instalment buyer, ended within a year, without the title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `since 1 July 2000 my partner held an interest in another home that either of us lived in` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my partner's home was in my earlier application, and I repaid that grant for not living there long enough` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Applicant facts`
`me from my answers` `I am applying as an individual` `my age on the commencement date` `the Commissioner has exempted me from the age requirement` `my citizenship or residence` `I am applying with another person` `the other applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` `I was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid` `that grant was paid back because it was not payable, with any penalty` `I held an interest in a home before 1 July 2000` `my interest was only as an instalment buyer, ended within a year, without the title` `since 1 July 2000 I held an interest in another home that I or my spouse lived in` `that home was in my earlier application, and I repaid that grant for not living there long enough` `my relationship` `my partner and I live together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis` `the years my partner and I have lived together as a couple` `my partner and I live apart` `the Commissioner is satisfied we have no intention of living together again` `the Commissioner is satisfied we intend to live together again` `my partner was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid` `my partner's grant was paid back because it was not payable, with any penalty` `my partner held an interest in a home before 1 July 2000` `my partner's interest was only as an instalment buyer, ended within a year, without the title` `since 1 July 2000 my partner held an interest in another home that either of us lived in` `my partner's home was in my earlier application, and I repaid that grant for not living there long enough` MEANS
    `Applicant facts` WITH
        `is a natural person`                                                  IS `I am applying as an individual`
        `age at the commencement date`                                         IS `my age on the commencement date`
        `the commissioner has exempted the applicant from the age requirement (s 11(2))` IS `the Commissioner has exempted me from the age requirement`
        `citizenship or residence`                                             IS `my citizenship or residence`
        `another joint applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` IS (`I am applying with another person` AND `the other applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`)
        `own earlier grant`                                                    IS `an earlier grant from my answers` `I was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid` `that grant was paid back because it was not payable, with any penalty`
        `own earlier property`                                                 IS `an earlier property from my answers` `I held an interest in a home before 1 July 2000` `my interest was only as an instalment buyer, ended within a year, without the title` `since 1 July 2000 I held an interest in another home that I or my spouse lived in` `that home was in my earlier application, and I repaid that grant for not living there long enough`
        `partner`                                                              IS `my partner from my answers` `my relationship` `my partner and I live together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis` `the years my partner and I have lived together as a couple` `my partner and I live apart` `the Commissioner is satisfied we have no intention of living together again` `the Commissioner is satisfied we intend to live together again`
        `partner's earlier grant`                                              IS `an earlier grant from my answers` `my partner was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid` `my partner's grant was paid back because it was not payable, with any penalty`
        `partner's earlier property`                                           IS `an earlier property from my answers` `my partner held an interest in a home before 1 July 2000` `my partner's interest was only as an instalment buyer, ended within a year, without the title` `since 1 July 2000 my partner held an interest in another home that either of us lived in` `my partner's home was in my earlier application, and I repaid that grant for not living there long enough`

GIVEN `the Commissioner has exempted me from living in the home`               IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner has approved a shorter period for me`                  IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shorter period, in months`                                          IS A NUMBER
      `the Commissioner has given me longer to move in`                        IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the longer time to move in`                             IS A DATE
      `the Commissioner has exempted me from the time to move in, as a joint applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another applicant on my application meets the residence requirement`   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Residence facts`
`my residence from my answers` `the Commissioner has exempted me from living in the home` `the Commissioner has approved a shorter period for me` `the shorter period, in months` `the Commissioner has given me longer to move in` `the last day of the longer time to move in` `the Commissioner has exempted me from the time to move in, as a joint applicant` `another applicant on my application meets the residence requirement` MEANS
    `Residence facts` WITH
        `the commissioner has exempted the applicant from s 15(1) (s 15(2)(b))` IS `the Commissioner has exempted me from living in the home`
        `the commissioner has approved a shorter period (s 15(2)(a))`          IS `the Commissioner has approved a shorter period for me`
        `the approved shorter period, in months`                                IS `the shorter period, in months`
        `the commissioner has approved a longer period to start (s 15(3))`     IS `the Commissioner has given me longer to move in`
        `the last day of the approved longer period to start`                   IS `the last day of the longer time to move in`
        `the commissioner has exempted the applicant from s 15(3) as a joint applicant (s 15(4))` IS `the Commissioner has exempted me from the time to move in, as a joint applicant`
        `another joint applicant complies with the residence requirement`      IS `another applicant on my application meets the residence requirement`

§§ `Part 2 Division 2 -- my home, my interest, my partner (ss 6, 8, 9)`

@export Is the home I am buying or building a new home for the first home owner grant (s 6)?
GIVEN `what I am doing` IS A `Kind of transaction` @desc What you are doing: buying a home (a contract to buy a home, or land the seller is building a home on), having a home built by a builder under a comprehensive home building contract, or building the home yourself as an owner builder
      `the home is a building fixed to land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home is (or, when built, will be) a building fixed to land (a caravan or a boat is not)
      `the home may lawfully be lived in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home may lawfully be used as a place to live (for example, it has the approvals needed to be occupied)
      `the home is suitable to live in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the building is suitable for use as a place to live
      `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anyone has lived in the home, or it has been sold as a home, before (for a home still to be built, answer no)
      `the sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises for GST` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a renovated home you are buying: whether the sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises under the GST Act, s 40-75(1)(b) (the seller or their adviser can say; if unsure, answer no)
      `as renovated, the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a renovated home you are buying: whether anyone has lived in the home, or it has been sold as a home, since it was renovated
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my home a new home` IF
    `it is a new home (s 6(2))` (`my home from my answers` `what I am doing` `the home is a building fixed to land` `the home may lawfully be lived in` `the home is suitable to live in` `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` `the sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises for GST` `as renovated, the home has been lived in or sold as a home before`)

@export Is the interest I will hold in the land a relevant interest, which makes me an owner of the home (ss 7 and 8; Regulation r 2)?
GIVEN `the kind of interest I will hold` IS A `Kind of interest` @desc The interest you will hold in the land the home is on: usually an estate in fee simple (you own the land); otherwise a life estate, a lease or licence from the Commonwealth or the State, an instalment purchase, company shares giving you a home, a right given by a relative to live in a house on their land, a mobile or manufactured home site, a long sublease, or a lease under the Aboriginal Land Act 1991 or Torres Strait Islander Land Act 1991
      `the Commissioner considers my licence or right gives me reasonable security of tenure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a licence or right of occupancy from the Commonwealth or the State: whether the Commissioner of State Revenue considers it gives you reasonable security of tenure
      `the Commissioner is satisfied my shares give me exclusive occupation of a home built before I acquired them, and are worth at least the company's interest in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for company shares: whether the Commissioner is satisfied of all three of these conditions
      `I will have a right to live there within a year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have, or will have within 1 year, a right to immediate occupation of the land (a lease to a tenant that delays this is disregarded when looking back at earlier homes, s 14(3))
      `I will hold it on trust for someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you will hold the interest as a trustee for someone else (an interest held on trust does not count)
      `my guardian holds it on trust for me because I am under a legal disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a guardian or trustee holds the interest on trust for you because you are under a legal disability (then you are treated as holding it)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my interest a relevant interest` IF
    `the person is an owner of the home (s 7)`
        (`Interest facts` WITH
            `the kind of interest`                                             IS `the kind of interest I will hold`
            `the commissioner considers the licence or right gives reasonable security of tenure` IS `the Commissioner considers my licence or right gives me reasonable security of tenure`
            `the commissioner is satisfied of the share conditions in s 8(1)(h)` IS `the Commissioner is satisfied my shares give me exclusive occupation of a home built before I acquired them, and are worth at least the company's interest in it`
            `the holder has, or will have within 1 year, a right to immediate occupation of the land` IS `I will have a right to live there within a year`
            `the person holds it subject to a trust`                           IS `I will hold it on trust for someone else`
            `a guardian holds it on trust for the person, who is under a legal disability` IS `my guardian holds it on trust for me because I am under a legal disability`)

@export Is my partner my spouse for the first home owner grant, so that their past grants and homes count against me (s 9)?
GIVEN `my relationship` IS A `Relationship` @desc Your relationship with your partner: married, in a civil partnership (a registered relationship), living together as a couple without being married or registered (de facto), or no partner
      `my partner and I live together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your partner now live together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis
      `the years my partner and I have lived together as a couple` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years you and your partner have lived together as a couple (a de facto partner counts only after 2 years)
      `my partner and I live apart` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your partner are now living apart
      `the Commissioner is satisfied we have no intention of living together again` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if married or in a civil partnership and living apart: whether the Commissioner is satisfied neither of you intends to live together as a couple again
      `the Commissioner is satisfied we intend to live together again` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if de facto and living apart: whether the Commissioner is satisfied you intend to live together as a couple again
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my partner my spouse for the grant` IF
    `the partner is the applicant's spouse (s 9)` (`my partner from my answers` `my relationship` `my partner and I live together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis` `the years my partner and I have lived together as a couple` `my partner and I live apart` `the Commissioner is satisfied we have no intention of living together again` `the Commissioner is satisfied we intend to live together again`)

§§ `Part 2 Division 2 and Part 3 Division 4 -- is my purchase or build eligible, and how much (ss 5, 20, 25EA, 25EB)`

DECLARE `My transaction answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes, it is an eligible transaction for a new home (s 5(1))`
    `yes, it is an eligible transaction for a home other than a new home (s 5(2))`
    `no, it is not an eligible transaction` HAS `because` IS A `Why the transaction is not eligible`
    `not covered: it commenced before 20 November 2023, and a version of the Act that is not deposited governs it`

@export Is the home I am buying or building an eligible transaction for the first home owner grant, under the $750,000 cap (s 5)?
GIVEN `what I am doing` IS A `Kind of transaction` @desc What you are doing: buying a home (a contract to buy a home, or land the seller is building a home on), having a home built by a builder under a comprehensive home building contract, or building the home yourself as an owner builder
      `the home is in Queensland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home (or the land it is being built on) is in Queensland
      `the home is a building fixed to land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home is (or, when built, will be) a building fixed to land (a caravan or a boat is not)
      `the home may lawfully be lived in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home may lawfully be used as a place to live (for example, it has the approvals needed to be occupied)
      `the home is suitable to live in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the building is suitable for use as a place to live
      `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anyone has lived in the home, or it has been sold as a home, before (for a home still to be built, answer no)
      `the sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises for GST` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a renovated home you are buying: whether the sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises under the GST Act, s 40-75(1)(b) (the seller or their adviser can say; if unsure, answer no)
      `as renovated, the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a renovated home you are buying: whether anyone has lived in the home, or it has been sold as a home, since it was renovated
      `I am buying land with the home on it, or that the seller will build on before completion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if buying: whether your contract is to buy land that already has the home on it, or that the seller will build the home on, at the seller's expense, before completion (buying vacant land and then signing a separate building contract is the building contract instead)
      `I own the land, or will own it on completion of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if having a home built or owner building: whether you own the land, or will own it when the building contract is completed
      `the commencement date` IS A DATE @desc The commencement date: the day the contract was made, or for an owner builder the day laying the foundations started (or another date the Commissioner considers appropriate)
      `the consideration` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: the price under a contract to buy; the total price of the building work under a building contract; or, for an owner builder, the actual cost of the work without anything for your own labour
      `the value of the home` IS A NUMBER @desc Only if buying: the value of the home itself in Australian dollars, ignoring any mortgage or other encumbrance and any arrangement that lowers it (if you have one value for home and land together, enter it in the land value and 0 here)
      `the value of the land` IS A NUMBER @desc The value in Australian dollars of the land (or your interest in it) on the commencement date, ignoring any mortgage or other encumbrance and any arrangement that lowers it
      `the Commissioner has found the contract is part of a scheme to get around the grant's limits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner of State Revenue is satisfied the contract is part of a scheme to get around the grant's limits or requirements (if nobody has said so, answer no)
      `an option or right to the contract was granted before 1 July 2000` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had an option to buy the home, the seller an option to make you buy it, or either party a right to require the building contract, granted before 1 July 2000
      `the contract replaces one made before 20 November 2023 for the same or a similar home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your contract replaces a contract made before 20 November 2023 to buy or build the same or a substantially similar home
      `an option or right to the contract was granted before 20 November 2023` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether such an option or right was granted before 20 November 2023
      `the Commissioner is satisfied the earlier option, right or contract is not part of a scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if there was such an earlier option, right or contract: whether the Commissioner is satisfied it is not part of a scheme (otherwise a scheme is presumed)
      `the Commissioner has found the contract is part of a scheme to get the 2023 to 2026 amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a contract made between 20 November 2023 and 30 June 2026: whether the Commissioner is satisfied it is part of a scheme to get the $30,000 grant of that period (if nobody has said so, answer no)
GIVETH A `My transaction answer`
DECIDE `Is my purchase or build an eligible transaction` IS
    IF (NOT (`the deposited text governs the transaction` `my transaction`))
    THEN `not covered: it commenced before 20 November 2023, and a version of the Act that is not deposited governs it`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the eligibility of the transaction (s 5)` `my transaction`
         WHEN `a new home eligible transaction (s 5(1))` THEN `yes, it is an eligible transaction for a new home (s 5(1))`
         WHEN `an eligible transaction for a home other than a new home (s 5(2))` THEN `yes, it is an eligible transaction for a home other than a new home (s 5(2))`
         WHEN `not an eligible transaction` `r` THEN `no, it is not an eligible transaction` `r`
    WHERE
        -- `the seller is building the home before completion` is read only by s 22A: FALSE here, a placeholder.
        `my transaction` MEANS
            `my transaction from my answers` `what I am doing` `the home is in Queensland` `the home is a building fixed to land` `the home may lawfully be lived in` `the home is suitable to live in` `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` `the sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises for GST` `as renovated, the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` `I am buying land with the home on it, or that the seller will build on before completion` FALSE `I own the land, or will own it on completion of the contract` `the commencement date` `the consideration` `the value of the home` `the value of the land` `the Commissioner has found the contract is part of a scheme to get around the grant's limits` `an option or right to the contract was granted before 1 July 2000` `the contract replaces one made before 20 November 2023 for the same or a similar home` `an option or right to the contract was granted before 20 November 2023` `the Commissioner is satisfied the earlier option, right or contract is not part of a scheme` `the Commissioner has found the contract is part of a scheme to get the 2023 to 2026 amount`

@export How much is the first home owner grant for the home I am buying or building, if it is payable (ss 20, 25EA and 25EB)?
GIVEN `what I am doing` IS A `Kind of transaction` @desc What you are doing: buying a home (a contract to buy a home, or land the seller is building a home on), having a home built by a builder under a comprehensive home building contract, or building the home yourself as an owner builder
      `the home is in Queensland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home (or the land it is being built on) is in Queensland
      `the home is a building fixed to land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home is (or, when built, will be) a building fixed to land (a caravan or a boat is not)
      `the home may lawfully be lived in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home may lawfully be used as a place to live (for example, it has the approvals needed to be occupied)
      `the home is suitable to live in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the building is suitable for use as a place to live
      `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anyone has lived in the home, or it has been sold as a home, before (for a home still to be built, answer no)
      `the sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises for GST` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a renovated home you are buying: whether the sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises under the GST Act, s 40-75(1)(b) (the seller or their adviser can say; if unsure, answer no)
      `as renovated, the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a renovated home you are buying: whether anyone has lived in the home, or it has been sold as a home, since it was renovated
      `I am buying land with the home on it, or that the seller will build on before completion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if buying: whether your contract is to buy land that already has the home on it, or that the seller will build the home on, at the seller's expense, before completion (buying vacant land and then signing a separate building contract is the building contract instead)
      `I own the land, or will own it on completion of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if having a home built or owner building: whether you own the land, or will own it when the building contract is completed
      `the commencement date` IS A DATE @desc The commencement date: the day the contract was made, or for an owner builder the day laying the foundations started (or another date the Commissioner considers appropriate)
      `the consideration` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: the price under a contract to buy; the total price of the building work under a building contract; or, for an owner builder, the actual cost of the work without anything for your own labour
      `the value of the home` IS A NUMBER @desc Only if buying: the value of the home itself in Australian dollars, ignoring any mortgage or other encumbrance and any arrangement that lowers it (if you have one value for home and land together, enter it in the land value and 0 here)
      `the value of the land` IS A NUMBER @desc The value in Australian dollars of the land (or your interest in it) on the commencement date, ignoring any mortgage or other encumbrance and any arrangement that lowers it
      `the Commissioner has found the contract is part of a scheme to get around the grant's limits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner of State Revenue is satisfied the contract is part of a scheme to get around the grant's limits or requirements (if nobody has said so, answer no)
      `an option or right to the contract was granted before 1 July 2000` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had an option to buy the home, the seller an option to make you buy it, or either party a right to require the building contract, granted before 1 July 2000
      `the contract replaces one made before 20 November 2023 for the same or a similar home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your contract replaces a contract made before 20 November 2023 to buy or build the same or a substantially similar home
      `an option or right to the contract was granted before 20 November 2023` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether such an option or right was granted before 20 November 2023
      `the Commissioner is satisfied the earlier option, right or contract is not part of a scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if there was such an earlier option, right or contract: whether the Commissioner is satisfied it is not part of a scheme (otherwise a scheme is presumed)
      `the Commissioner has found the contract is part of a scheme to get the 2023 to 2026 amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a contract made between 20 November 2023 and 30 June 2026: whether the Commissioner is satisfied it is part of a scheme to get the $30,000 grant of that period (if nobody has said so, answer no)
GIVETH AN `Amount answer`
DECIDE `How much is the grant for my home` IS
    `the amount of the grant for` (`my transaction from my answers` `what I am doing` `the home is in Queensland` `the home is a building fixed to land` `the home may lawfully be lived in` `the home is suitable to live in` `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` `the sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises for GST` `as renovated, the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` `I am buying land with the home on it, or that the seller will build on before completion` FALSE `I own the land, or will own it on completion of the contract` `the commencement date` `the consideration` `the value of the home` `the value of the land` `the Commissioner has found the contract is part of a scheme to get around the grant's limits` `an option or right to the contract was granted before 1 July 2000` `the contract replaces one made before 20 November 2023 for the same or a similar home` `an option or right to the contract was granted before 20 November 2023` `the Commissioner is satisfied the earlier option, right or contract is not part of a scheme` `the Commissioner has found the contract is part of a scheme to get the 2023 to 2026 amount`)

§§ `Part 3 Division 2 -- am I eligible (ss 11 to 14)`

-- A joint applicant asks this from their own seat; the payable question takes their answer.
@export Do I meet eligibility criteria 1 to 4 for the first home owner grant: age, citizenship or residence, no earlier grant, no earlier home (ss 11 to 14)?
GIVEN `I am applying as an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are applying as a person in your own right (not as a company, or as trustee of a trust)
      `my age on the commencement date` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years on the commencement date (the day the contract was made, or the day the foundations started)
      `the Commissioner has exempted me from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if under 18: whether the Commissioner of State Revenue has exempted you from the requirement to be 18
      `my citizenship or residence` IS A `Citizenship or residence` @desc Whether you are an Australian citizen, the holder of a permanent visa, a New Zealand citizen holding a special category visa, or none of these
      `I am applying with another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are applying jointly with another person (everyone who will own the home must apply)
      `the other applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if applying jointly: whether at least one other applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident
      `I was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been a party to an earlier first home owner grant application, in Queensland or another State, on which a grant was paid
      `that grant was paid back because it was not payable, with any penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if so: whether that grant was later paid back because it was not payable after all, together with any penalty
      `I held an interest in a home before 1 July 2000` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before 1 July 2000, you owned (or held another listed interest in) land in Australia with a house or other residence on it, in Queensland or under another State's first home owner law
      `my interest was only as an instalment buyer, ended within a year, without the title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if so: whether that interest was only as a buyer under an instalment contract that ended within 1 year, without you getting the title
      `since 1 July 2000 I held an interest in another home that I or my spouse lived in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, from 1 July 2000 until you apply, you owned (or held another listed interest in) a residential property other than this one that you or your spouse lived in at any time since 1 July 2000
      `that home was in my earlier application, and I repaid that grant for not living there long enough` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if so: whether that other home was the subject of your own earlier grant application, and you repaid that grant because you did not meet the residence requirement
      `my relationship` IS A `Relationship` @desc Your relationship with your partner: married, in a civil partnership (a registered relationship), living together as a couple without being married or registered (de facto), or no partner
      `my partner and I live together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your partner now live together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis
      `the years my partner and I have lived together as a couple` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years you and your partner have lived together as a couple (a de facto partner counts only after 2 years)
      `my partner and I live apart` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your partner are now living apart
      `the Commissioner is satisfied we have no intention of living together again` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if married or in a civil partnership and living apart: whether the Commissioner is satisfied neither of you intends to live together as a couple again
      `the Commissioner is satisfied we intend to live together again` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if de facto and living apart: whether the Commissioner is satisfied you intend to live together as a couple again
      `my partner was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your partner has been a party to an earlier first home owner grant application, in Queensland or another State, on which a grant was paid
      `my partner's grant was paid back because it was not payable, with any penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if so: whether that grant was later paid back because it was not payable after all, together with any penalty
      `my partner held an interest in a home before 1 July 2000` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before 1 July 2000, your partner owned (or held another listed interest in) land in Australia with a residence on it
      `my partner's interest was only as an instalment buyer, ended within a year, without the title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if so: whether that interest was only as a buyer under an instalment contract that ended within 1 year, without your partner getting the title
      `since 1 July 2000 my partner held an interest in another home that either of us lived in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, from 1 July 2000 until you apply, your partner owned (or held another listed interest in) a residential property other than this one that either of you lived in at any time since 1 July 2000
      `my partner's home was in my earlier application, and I repaid that grant for not living there long enough` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if so: whether that home was the subject of your own earlier grant application, and you repaid that grant because you did not meet the residence requirement
GIVETH A `Criteria answer`
DECIDE `Do I meet eligibility criteria 1 to 4` IS
    `the criteria 1 to 4 answer for` (`me from my answers` `I am applying as an individual` `my age on the commencement date` `the Commissioner has exempted me from the age requirement` `my citizenship or residence` `I am applying with another person` `the other applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` `I was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid` `that grant was paid back because it was not payable, with any penalty` `I held an interest in a home before 1 July 2000` `my interest was only as an instalment buyer, ended within a year, without the title` `since 1 July 2000 I held an interest in another home that I or my spouse lived in` `that home was in my earlier application, and I repaid that grant for not living there long enough` `my relationship` `my partner and I live together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis` `the years my partner and I have lived together as a couple` `my partner and I live apart` `the Commissioner is satisfied we have no intention of living together again` `the Commissioner is satisfied we intend to live together again` `my partner was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid` `my partner's grant was paid back because it was not payable, with any penalty` `my partner held an interest in a home before 1 July 2000` `my partner's interest was only as an instalment buyer, ended within a year, without the title` `since 1 July 2000 my partner held an interest in another home that either of us lived in` `my partner's home was in my earlier application, and I repaid that grant for not living there long enough`)

§§ `Part 3 Divisions 1 and 3 -- applying, and whether the grant is payable (ss 10, 16, 17; schedule, completed; Regulation rr 3, 6)`

@export Has my purchase or build been completed, which the grant needs (schedule, completed; Regulation r 6)?
GIVEN `what I am doing` IS A `Kind of transaction` @desc What you are doing: buying a home, having a home built under a comprehensive home building contract, or building as an owner builder
      `I am entitled to possession of the home under the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if buying: whether you have become entitled to possession of the home under the contract (usually at settlement)
      `I am to get a registered title to the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if buying: whether you are to obtain a registered title to the land the home is on
      `my title is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if buying with a registered title: whether your title has been registered
      `the building is ready to live in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if building: whether the building is ready for occupation as a home
      `a final inspection certificate has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if building: whether a final inspection certificate under the Building Act 1975 has been issued for the building
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my purchase or build been completed` IF
    `the transaction has been completed` `what I am doing` (`my completion from my answers` `I am entitled to possession of the home under the contract` `I am to get a registered title to the land` `my title is registered` `the building is ready to live in` `a final inspection certificate has been issued`)

GIVEN `I am entitled to possession of the home under the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am to get a registered title to the land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my title is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the building is ready to live in` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a final inspection certificate has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Completion facts`
`my completion from my answers` `I am entitled to possession of the home under the contract` `I am to get a registered title to the land` `my title is registered` `the building is ready to live in` `a final inspection certificate has been issued` MEANS
    `Completion facts` WITH
        `the purchaser is entitled to possession of the home under the contract` IS `I am entitled to possession of the home under the contract`
        `the purchaser is to obtain a registered title to the land`             IS `I am to get a registered title to the land`
        `the purchaser's title is registered`                                    IS `my title is registered`
        `the building is ready for occupation as a home`                         IS `the building is ready to live in`
        `a final inspection certificate under the Building Act 1975 has been issued` IS `a final inspection certificate has been issued`

GIVEN `the other person will own the home on completion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is applying with me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my interest is one declared by Regulation r 2(1), and the other person holds another interest in the land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is the housing chief executive under the Pathways Shared Equity Loan scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the housing chief executive holds or will hold no more than 40% of the land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the housing department finances my purchase or build` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a tenant of the home` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Other owner facts`
`the other owner from my answers` `the other person will own the home on completion` `the other person is applying with me` `my interest is one declared by Regulation r 2(1), and the other person holds another interest in the land` `the other person is the housing chief executive under the Pathways Shared Equity Loan scheme` `the housing chief executive holds or will hold no more than 40% of the land` `the housing department finances my purchase or build` `I am a tenant of the home` MEANS
    `Other owner facts` WITH
        `will be an owner of the home on completion`                            IS `the other person will own the home on completion`
        `is an applicant`                                                       IS `the other person is applying with me`
        `the applicant's interest is one declared by Regulation r 2(1), and this person holds another relevant interest in the land` IS `my interest is one declared by Regulation r 2(1), and the other person holds another interest in the land`
        `is the housing chief executive under the Pathways Shared Equity Loan scheme` IS `the other person is the housing chief executive under the Pathways Shared Equity Loan scheme`
        `holds or will hold not more than 40% of the fee simple`                IS `the housing chief executive holds or will hold no more than 40% of the land`
        `the transaction is financed by the housing department`                 IS `the housing department finances my purchase or build`
        `the applicant is a tenant of the home`                                 IS `I am a tenant of the home`

@export Must this other person who will own the home join my application for the grant (s 17; Regulation r 3)?
GIVEN `the other person will own the home on completion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other person is, or will be on completion, an owner of the home (holds a relevant interest in the land, such as a share of the title)
      `my interest is one declared by Regulation r 2(1), and the other person holds another interest in the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your own interest is one the Regulation adds (a right from a relative to live on their land, a mobile or manufactured home site, a long sublease, or an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander land lease) and the other person holds another interest in the same land, such as the relative or park owner who owns it
      `the other person is the housing chief executive under the Pathways Shared Equity Loan scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other owner is the chief executive of the housing department, under the Pathways Shared Equity Loan scheme
      `the housing chief executive holds or will hold no more than 40% of the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for that scheme: whether the housing chief executive holds, or will hold, not more than 40% of the fee simple in the land
      `the housing department finances my purchase or build` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for that scheme: whether the housing department finances the purchase or build
      `I am a tenant of the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for that scheme: whether you are a tenant of the home
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must this other owner join my application` IF
    `the person is an interested person (s 17(2), Regulation r 3)` (`the other owner from my answers` `the other person will own the home on completion` FALSE `my interest is one declared by Regulation r 2(1), and the other person holds another interest in the land` `the other person is the housing chief executive under the Pathways Shared Equity Loan scheme` `the housing chief executive holds or will hold no more than 40% of the land` `the housing department finances my purchase or build` `I am a tenant of the home`)

@export Is the first home owner grant payable on my application: an eligible transaction, completed, every applicant meeting criteria 1 to 4, and every owner applying (s 10)?
GIVEN `what I am doing` IS A `Kind of transaction` @desc What you are doing: buying a home (a contract to buy a home, or land the seller is building a home on), having a home built by a builder under a comprehensive home building contract, or building the home yourself as an owner builder
      `the home is in Queensland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home (or the land it is being built on) is in Queensland
      `the home is a building fixed to land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home is (or, when built, will be) a building fixed to land (a caravan or a boat is not)
      `the home may lawfully be lived in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home may lawfully be used as a place to live (for example, it has the approvals needed to be occupied)
      `the home is suitable to live in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the building is suitable for use as a place to live
      `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anyone has lived in the home, or it has been sold as a home, before (for a home still to be built, answer no)
      `the sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises for GST` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a renovated home you are buying: whether the sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises under the GST Act, s 40-75(1)(b) (the seller or their adviser can say; if unsure, answer no)
      `as renovated, the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a renovated home you are buying: whether anyone has lived in the home, or it has been sold as a home, since it was renovated
      `I am buying land with the home on it, or that the seller will build on before completion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if buying: whether your contract is to buy land that already has the home on it, or that the seller will build the home on, at the seller's expense, before completion (buying vacant land and then signing a separate building contract is the building contract instead)
      `I own the land, or will own it on completion of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if having a home built or owner building: whether you own the land, or will own it when the building contract is completed
      `the commencement date` IS A DATE @desc The commencement date: the day the contract was made, or for an owner builder the day laying the foundations started (or another date the Commissioner considers appropriate)
      `the consideration` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars: the price under a contract to buy; the total price of the building work under a building contract; or, for an owner builder, the actual cost of the work without anything for your own labour
      `the value of the home` IS A NUMBER @desc Only if buying: the value of the home itself in Australian dollars, ignoring any mortgage or other encumbrance and any arrangement that lowers it (if you have one value for home and land together, enter it in the land value and 0 here)
      `the value of the land` IS A NUMBER @desc The value in Australian dollars of the land (or your interest in it) on the commencement date, ignoring any mortgage or other encumbrance and any arrangement that lowers it
      `the Commissioner has found the contract is part of a scheme to get around the grant's limits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner of State Revenue is satisfied the contract is part of a scheme to get around the grant's limits or requirements (if nobody has said so, answer no)
      `an option or right to the contract was granted before 1 July 2000` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had an option to buy the home, the seller an option to make you buy it, or either party a right to require the building contract, granted before 1 July 2000
      `the contract replaces one made before 20 November 2023 for the same or a similar home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your contract replaces a contract made before 20 November 2023 to buy or build the same or a substantially similar home
      `an option or right to the contract was granted before 20 November 2023` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether such an option or right was granted before 20 November 2023
      `the Commissioner is satisfied the earlier option, right or contract is not part of a scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if there was such an earlier option, right or contract: whether the Commissioner is satisfied it is not part of a scheme (otherwise a scheme is presumed)
      `the Commissioner has found the contract is part of a scheme to get the 2023 to 2026 amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a contract made between 20 November 2023 and 30 June 2026: whether the Commissioner is satisfied it is part of a scheme to get the $30,000 grant of that period (if nobody has said so, answer no)
      `I am entitled to possession of the home under the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if buying: whether you have become entitled to possession of the home under the contract (usually at settlement)
      `I am to get a registered title to the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if buying: whether you are to obtain a registered title to the land the home is on
      `my title is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if buying with a registered title: whether your title has been registered
      `the building is ready to live in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if building: whether the building is ready for occupation as a home
      `a final inspection certificate has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if building: whether a final inspection certificate under the Building Act 1975 has been issued for the building
      `I am applying as an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are applying as a person in your own right (not as a company, or as trustee of a trust)
      `my age on the commencement date` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years on the commencement date (the day the contract was made, or the day the foundations started)
      `the Commissioner has exempted me from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if under 18: whether the Commissioner of State Revenue has exempted you from the requirement to be 18
      `my citizenship or residence` IS A `Citizenship or residence` @desc Whether you are an Australian citizen, the holder of a permanent visa, a New Zealand citizen holding a special category visa, or none of these
      `I am applying with another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are applying jointly with another person (everyone who will own the home must apply)
      `the other applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if applying jointly: whether at least one other applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident
      `I was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been a party to an earlier first home owner grant application, in Queensland or another State, on which a grant was paid
      `that grant was paid back because it was not payable, with any penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if so: whether that grant was later paid back because it was not payable after all, together with any penalty
      `I held an interest in a home before 1 July 2000` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before 1 July 2000, you owned (or held another listed interest in) land in Australia with a house or other residence on it, in Queensland or under another State's first home owner law
      `my interest was only as an instalment buyer, ended within a year, without the title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if so: whether that interest was only as a buyer under an instalment contract that ended within 1 year, without you getting the title
      `since 1 July 2000 I held an interest in another home that I or my spouse lived in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, from 1 July 2000 until you apply, you owned (or held another listed interest in) a residential property other than this one that you or your spouse lived in at any time since 1 July 2000
      `that home was in my earlier application, and I repaid that grant for not living there long enough` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if so: whether that other home was the subject of your own earlier grant application, and you repaid that grant because you did not meet the residence requirement
      `my relationship` IS A `Relationship` @desc Your relationship with your partner: married, in a civil partnership (a registered relationship), living together as a couple without being married or registered (de facto), or no partner
      `my partner and I live together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your partner now live together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis
      `the years my partner and I have lived together as a couple` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years you and your partner have lived together as a couple (a de facto partner counts only after 2 years)
      `my partner and I live apart` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your partner are now living apart
      `the Commissioner is satisfied we have no intention of living together again` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if married or in a civil partnership and living apart: whether the Commissioner is satisfied neither of you intends to live together as a couple again
      `the Commissioner is satisfied we intend to live together again` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if de facto and living apart: whether the Commissioner is satisfied you intend to live together as a couple again
      `my partner was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your partner has been a party to an earlier first home owner grant application, in Queensland or another State, on which a grant was paid
      `my partner's grant was paid back because it was not payable, with any penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if so: whether that grant was later paid back because it was not payable after all, together with any penalty
      `my partner held an interest in a home before 1 July 2000` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before 1 July 2000, your partner owned (or held another listed interest in) land in Australia with a residence on it
      `my partner's interest was only as an instalment buyer, ended within a year, without the title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if so: whether that interest was only as a buyer under an instalment contract that ended within 1 year, without your partner getting the title
      `since 1 July 2000 my partner held an interest in another home that either of us lived in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, from 1 July 2000 until you apply, your partner owned (or held another listed interest in) a residential property other than this one that either of you lived in at any time since 1 July 2000
      `my partner's home was in my earlier application, and I repaid that grant for not living there long enough` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if so: whether that home was the subject of your own earlier grant application, and you repaid that grant because you did not meet the residence requirement
      `the other applicant meets criteria 1 to 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if applying jointly: whether the other applicant meets eligibility criteria 1 to 4 (they can answer "Do I meet eligibility criteria 1 to 4" for themselves)
      `someone else will own the home on completion and is not applying with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anyone else is, or will be on completion, an owner of the home without being an applicant
      `my interest is one declared by Regulation r 2(1), and the other person holds another interest in the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if so: whether your own interest is one the Regulation adds (a right from a relative to live on their land, a mobile or manufactured home site, a long sublease, or an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander land lease) and that person holds another interest in the same land
      `the other person is the housing chief executive under the Pathways Shared Equity Loan scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if so: whether that person is the chief executive of the housing department, under the Pathways Shared Equity Loan scheme
      `the housing chief executive holds or will hold no more than 40% of the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for that scheme: whether the housing chief executive holds, or will hold, not more than 40% of the fee simple in the land
      `the housing department finances my purchase or build` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for that scheme: whether the housing department finances the purchase or build
      `I am a tenant of the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for that scheme: whether you are a tenant of the home
      `a grant has already been paid for this purchase or build` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a first home owner grant has already been paid for this same purchase or build (only one is payable)
      `the Commissioner has refused or reversed my application for a disqualifying arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has refused or reversed your application because of a disqualifying arrangement (s 69A: for example a relative who would not qualify funds the home and uses it too)
GIVETH A `Payable answer`
DECIDE `Is the grant payable on my application` IS
    `whether the grant is payable (s 10)`
        (`Application facts` WITH
            `the transaction`                                                   IS `my transaction from my answers` `what I am doing` `the home is in Queensland` `the home is a building fixed to land` `the home may lawfully be lived in` `the home is suitable to live in` `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` `the sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises for GST` `as renovated, the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` `I am buying land with the home on it, or that the seller will build on before completion` FALSE `I own the land, or will own it on completion of the contract` `the commencement date` `the consideration` `the value of the home` `the value of the land` `the Commissioner has found the contract is part of a scheme to get around the grant's limits` `an option or right to the contract was granted before 1 July 2000` `the contract replaces one made before 20 November 2023 for the same or a similar home` `an option or right to the contract was granted before 20 November 2023` `the Commissioner is satisfied the earlier option, right or contract is not part of a scheme` `the Commissioner has found the contract is part of a scheme to get the 2023 to 2026 amount`
            `the completion`                                                    IS `my completion from my answers` `I am entitled to possession of the home under the contract` `I am to get a registered title to the land` `my title is registered` `the building is ready to live in` `a final inspection certificate has been issued`
            `the main applicant`                                                IS `me from my answers` `I am applying as an individual` `my age on the commencement date` `the Commissioner has exempted me from the age requirement` `my citizenship or residence` `I am applying with another person` `the other applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` `I was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid` `that grant was paid back because it was not payable, with any penalty` `I held an interest in a home before 1 July 2000` `my interest was only as an instalment buyer, ended within a year, without the title` `since 1 July 2000 I held an interest in another home that I or my spouse lived in` `that home was in my earlier application, and I repaid that grant for not living there long enough` `my relationship` `my partner and I live together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis` `the years my partner and I have lived together as a couple` `my partner and I live apart` `the Commissioner is satisfied we have no intention of living together again` `the Commissioner is satisfied we intend to live together again` `my partner was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid` `my partner's grant was paid back because it was not payable, with any penalty` `my partner held an interest in a home before 1 July 2000` `my partner's interest was only as an instalment buyer, ended within a year, without the title` `since 1 July 2000 my partner held an interest in another home that either of us lived in` `my partner's home was in my earlier application, and I repaid that grant for not living there long enough`
            `there is another joint applicant`                                  IS `I am applying with another person`
            `the other joint applicant meets criteria 1 to 4`                   IS `the other applicant meets criteria 1 to 4`
            `the other owner`                                                   IS `the other owner from my answers` `someone else will own the home on completion and is not applying with me` FALSE `my interest is one declared by Regulation r 2(1), and the other person holds another interest in the land` `the other person is the housing chief executive under the Pathways Shared Equity Loan scheme` `the housing chief executive holds or will hold no more than 40% of the land` `the housing department finances my purchase or build` `I am a tenant of the home`
            `a grant has already been paid for the same transaction`            IS `a grant has already been paid for this purchase or build`
            `the commissioner has refused or reversed it for a disqualifying arrangement (s 69A)` IS `the Commissioner has refused or reversed my application for a disqualifying arrangement`)

@export What is the last day I can apply for the first home owner grant, unless the Commissioner allows a late application (s 16)?
GIVEN `the completion date` IS A DATE @desc The day your purchase or build was (or will be) completed: settlement for a purchase, or the day the building was ready to live in with its final inspection certificate
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day I can apply` IS `the last day of the application period` `the completion date`

@export Can I apply for the first home owner grant on this day (s 16(3), (4))?
GIVEN `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you make (or made) the application
      `the commencement date` IS A DATE @desc The commencement date: the day the contract was made, or for an owner builder the day laying the foundations started
      `the completion date` IS A DATE @desc The day your purchase or build was (or will be) completed
      `the Commissioner has allowed me to apply outside the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner of State Revenue has allowed you to apply before the commencement date or more than 1 year after completion
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I apply on this day` IF
    `the application may be made on that day (s 16(3), (4))` `the day I apply` `the commencement date` `the completion date` `the Commissioner has allowed me to apply outside the period`

§§ `s 15 -- moving in and staying (criterion 5)`

DECLARE `My residence requirement` IS ONE OF
    `I am exempt from living in the home (s 15(2)(b))`
    `move in by, and stay for` HAS `the last day to move in` IS A DATE
                                   `months` IS A NUMBER
    `no deadline to move in (s 15(4)), but stay for` HAS `months` IS A NUMBER

@export By when must I move into the home, and for how long must I live there as my principal place of residence (s 15)?
GIVEN `the completion date` IS A DATE @desc The day your purchase or build was (or will be) completed: settlement for a purchase, or the day the building was ready to live in with its final inspection certificate
      `the Commissioner has exempted me from living in the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner of State Revenue has exempted you, for good reasons, from having to live in the home
      `the Commissioner has approved a shorter period for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has approved, for good reasons, a period shorter than 6 months
      `the shorter period, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc Only if so: the shorter period, in months
      `the Commissioner has given me longer to move in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has approved a longer time than 1 year after completion to move in
      `the last day of the longer time to move in` IS A DATE @desc Only if so: the last day of that longer time
      `the Commissioner has exempted me from the time to move in, as a joint applicant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if applying jointly: whether the Commissioner has exempted you, for good reasons, from the time limit to move in (s 15(4))
      `another applicant on my application meets the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if applying jointly: whether at least one other applicant meets the residence requirement
GIVETH A `My residence requirement`
DECIDE `By when must I move in, and for how long` IS
    IF `my residence`'s `the commissioner has exempted the applicant from s 15(1) (s 15(2)(b))`
    THEN `I am exempt from living in the home (s 15(2)(b))`
    ELSE IF `the start deadline applies to the applicant` `my residence`
         THEN `move in by, and stay for` (`the last day to start occupying the home` `my residence` `the completion date`) (`the months the applicant must occupy the home` `my residence`)
         ELSE `no deadline to move in (s 15(4)), but stay for` (`the months the applicant must occupy the home` `my residence`)
    WHERE
        `my residence` MEANS `my residence from my answers` `the Commissioner has exempted me from living in the home` `the Commissioner has approved a shorter period for me` `the shorter period, in months` `the Commissioner has given me longer to move in` `the last day of the longer time to move in` `the Commissioner has exempted me from the time to move in, as a joint applicant` `another applicant on my application meets the residence requirement`

@export Have I met the residence requirements for the first home owner grant: moved in on time and lived there for the required continuous period (s 15)?
GIVEN `the completion date` IS A DATE @desc The day your purchase or build was completed: settlement for a purchase, or the day the building was ready to live in with its final inspection certificate
      `the Commissioner has exempted me from living in the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner of State Revenue has exempted you, for good reasons, from having to live in the home
      `the Commissioner has approved a shorter period for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has approved, for good reasons, a period shorter than 6 months
      `the shorter period, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc Only if so: the shorter period, in months
      `the Commissioner has given me longer to move in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has approved a longer time than 1 year after completion to move in
      `the last day of the longer time to move in` IS A DATE @desc Only if so: the last day of that longer time
      `the Commissioner has exempted me from the time to move in, as a joint applicant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if applying jointly: whether the Commissioner has exempted you, for good reasons, from the time limit to move in (s 15(4))
      `another applicant on my application meets the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if applying jointly: whether at least one other applicant meets the residence requirement
      `I have moved in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have started to live in the home as your principal place of residence
      `the day I moved in` IS A DATE @desc Only if so: the first day of the continuous period you lived there as your principal place of residence
      `I have since moved out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if so: whether that continuous period has ended (you moved out, or the home stopped being your principal place of residence)
      `the first day I no longer lived there` IS A DATE @desc Only if so: the first day the home was no longer your principal place of residence
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day on which you are asking (usually today)
GIVETH A `Residence answer`
DECIDE `Have I met the residence requirements` IS
    `the residence answer`
        (`my residence from my answers` `the Commissioner has exempted me from living in the home` `the Commissioner has approved a shorter period for me` `the shorter period, in months` `the Commissioner has given me longer to move in` `the last day of the longer time to move in` `the Commissioner has exempted me from the time to move in, as a joint applicant` `another applicant on my application meets the residence requirement`)
        (`Occupation facts` WITH
            `has started to occupy the home as principal place of residence`   IS `I have moved in`
            `the first day of the continuous period of occupation`              IS `the day I moved in`
            `that period of occupation has ended`                               IS `I have since moved out`
            `the first day the home was no longer the principal place of residence` IS `the first day I no longer lived there`)
        `the completion date`
        `the day I am asking about`

§§ `s 22, s 22A -- if I was paid before meeting a requirement (only if the grant was paid early or in anticipation)`

@export If my grant was paid in anticipation and I will not meet the residence requirements, by when must I tell the Commissioner in writing and repay it (s 22(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the completion date` IS A DATE @desc The day your purchase or build was completed
      `the Commissioner has approved a shorter period for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has approved, for good reasons, a period shorter than 6 months
      `the shorter period, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc Only if so: the shorter period, in months
      `the Commissioner has given me longer to move in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has approved a longer time than 1 year after completion to move in
      `the last day of the longer time to move in` IS A DATE @desc Only if so: the last day of that longer time
      `the day it first became apparent I would not meet them` IS A DATE @desc The first day it became apparent you would not meet the residence requirements in the time allowed (for example the day you moved out early, or decided not to move in)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I notify and repay for not living there` IS
    `the last day to notify and repay (s 22(2))`
        (`the relevant date (s 22(3))`
            (`my residence from my answers` FALSE `the Commissioner has approved a shorter period for me` `the shorter period, in months` `the Commissioner has given me longer to move in` `the last day of the longer time to move in` FALSE FALSE)
            `the completion date`
            `the day it first became apparent I would not meet them`)

DECLARE `My s 22A answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: s 22A does not apply to me`
    `yes: give the Commissioner written notice and repay the grant by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

@export My grant was paid before completion and my home turned out to be worth $750,000 or more with the land: must I give notice and repay, and by when (s 22A)?
GIVEN `what I am doing` IS A `Kind of transaction` @desc What you are doing: buying a home, having a home built under a comprehensive home building contract, or building as an owner builder
      `the seller is building the home before completion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if buying: whether the contract is for land on which the seller is to build the home, at the seller's expense, before completion
      `the grant was paid to me before completion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the grant was paid to you before your purchase or build was completed
      `the consideration` IS A NUMBER @desc In Australian dollars, as it turned out on completion: the total price of the building work, or for an owner builder the actual cost of the work without your own labour (for a purchase, as in the contract)
      `the value of the home` IS A NUMBER @desc Only if buying: the value of the completed home itself in Australian dollars, ignoring any mortgage or other encumbrance and any arrangement that lowers it
      `the value of the land` IS A NUMBER @desc The value in Australian dollars of the land on the commencement date, ignoring any mortgage or other encumbrance and any arrangement that lowers it
      `the completion date` IS A DATE @desc The day your purchase or build was completed
GIVETH A `My s 22A answer`
DECIDE `Must I notify and repay because my home is over the cap on completion` IS
    IF `s 22A applies` `my transaction` `the grant was paid to me before completion`
    THEN `yes: give the Commissioner written notice and repay the grant by` (`the last day to notify and repay (s 22A(2))` `the completion date`)
    ELSE `no: s 22A does not apply to me`
    WHERE
        -- s 22A reads only the kind, the vendor-build fact, the consideration and the values. Every other field is a
        -- placeholder no rule here reads: TRUE for the facts of a home, FALSE for the schemes, 1 July 2026 for the date.
        `my transaction` MEANS
            `my transaction from my answers` `what I am doing` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `the seller is building the home before completion` TRUE `1 July 2026` `the consideration` `the value of the home` `the value of the land` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§§ `Part 4 Division 3 -- what I can be made to repay, and the charge on my home (ss 47 to 49; Regulation r 4)`

@export If the Commissioner says my grant was paid in error, what is the most penalty that can be added on top of repaying it (s 47(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the amount paid in error` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount, in Australian dollars, the Commissioner's notice says was paid in error (usually the grant)
      `it was paid because of a false or misleading document or statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was paid because of a false or misleading document or statement given for the application (ss 42, 43)
      `I have not made a repayment required of me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have failed to make a repayment the Commissioner required, or that the conditions of the grant required
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most penalty on top of repaying` IS
    `the most penalty the commissioner may impose (s 47(2), (3))` `the amount paid in error` `it was paid because of a false or misleading document or statement` `I have not made a repayment required of me`

@export What is the most I can be fined for failing, without reasonable excuse, to give notice and repay the grant as required (ss 22(5), 22A(2), 23(4))?
GIVEN `the value of a penalty unit` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of one penalty unit in Queensland, in Australian dollars, on the day of the failure (set under the Penalties and Sentences Act 1992; not part of this Act)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for not notifying and repaying` IS
    `the maximum penalty in penalty units (ss 22(5), 22A(2), 23(4))` TIMES `the value of a penalty unit`

@export If two or more of us must repay, is each of us liable for the whole amount (s 48(2))?
GIVEN `how many of us must repay` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people the requirement to repay or pay applies to (for example both joint applicants)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is each of us liable for the whole amount` IF `the liability is joint and several (s 48(2))` `how many of us must repay`

@export If I pay what I owe by instalments, what is the most interest a year the arrangement can charge (s 48(4), (5); Regulation r 4)?
GIVEN `the bank bill yield rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The Reserve Bank of Australia's monthly average yield of 90-day bank accepted bills for May of the previous financial year, in per cent (for example 3.85)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What interest can my instalment arrangement charge` IS `the instalment interest rate, per cent a year (Regulation r 4)` `the bank bill yield rate`

@export Is the amount I must repay a first charge on my interest in the home's land, ahead of my mortgage (s 49)?
GIVEN `I must repay an amount or pay a penalty under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are liable to repay the grant, or to pay a penalty amount, under the conditions of the grant or a requirement of the Act
      `I have an interest in the land the home is on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold an interest (such as ownership) in the land on which the home is fixed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I owe a charge on my home` IF
    `the liability is a first charge on the interest in the land (s 49)` `I must repay an amount or pay a penalty under the Act` `I have an interest in the land the home is on`

§§ `Part 5 -- objecting to a decision, and review by QCAT (ss 56 to 59) -- only if a decision has gone against me`

@export By when must I lodge a written objection to the Commissioner's decision on my application, or to a repayment notice (s 56)?
GIVEN `the day I received the notice of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the Commissioner's written notice of the decision (refusing your application, varying it, or requiring repayment)
      `the Commissioner has extended my time to object` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner, satisfied you had a reasonable excuse, has extended the time to object
      `the last day of the extended time` IS A DATE @desc Only if so: the last day of the extended time
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I object` IS
    `the last day to object` `the day I received the notice of the decision` `the Commissioner has extended my time to object` `the last day of the extended time`

@export By when must I apply to QCAT to review the Commissioner's decision on my objection (s 59)?
GIVEN `the day I received the notice of the decision on my objection` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the Commissioner's written notice of the decision on your objection
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I apply to QCAT` IS
    `the last day to apply to QCAT` `the day I received the notice of the decision on my objection`
